<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54077" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταιτι-άομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>accuse, arraign</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.14
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί σαυτὸν ἀδικῶν τὴν τύχην
				καταιτιᾷ</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				618
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					57.27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰς ἀσεβείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					68.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				8.13.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span> c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χρήματα εἰληφέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					104.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.1.4
			</span></i>(v.l.): abs. in med.sense, <i>accuse one another</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.92
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ́</span>:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				64
			</span></i>(<i>a</i>).<i><span class="en">
				84
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc. rei, <i>lay</i> something <i>to one's charge,
			impute</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμαθίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.42
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταιτιώμενος ταῦτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.118
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			aor. 1
			part.
			
				Pass.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταιτιαθείς</span> in pass. sense,
				<i>accused person, defendant</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ
			κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.32.11
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐκ τοῦ Περσικοῦ πολέμου
			κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.5.4
			</span></i>: c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταιτιαθεὶς ταῦτα πρᾶξαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					1.1.32
				</span></i>
			; so also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ κατῃτιαμένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					32.3.14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατῃτιᾶσθαι τὴν κλοπήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					4.31
				</span></i>
			.</div>
